<title>SWITZERLAND: CS reports H1 1997 net up 70 pct.</title>
<headline>CS reports H1 1997 net up 70 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Suisse Group said in a preliminary release of first half results that it expected net profit to be around 1.410 billion Swiss francs for the period, a rise of about 70 percent versus 1996 mid-year results.</p>
<p>It said that the results, after minority interests and implementation of a new credit risk management framework, were equal to about 7.25 Swiss francs per share.</p>
<p>It estimated its return on equity for the half year period to be about 17 percent.</p>
</text>
